111| \begin{definition}[Exo and endo cyclisations]\label{def:b3:radicals-carbenes:cyclisation}
112| In an \emph{exo cyclisation}\index{exo cyclisation} the bond that is broken (or
113| the $\pi$ bond attacked) ends up outside the new ring; in an \emph{endo
114| cyclisation}\index{endo cyclisation}, inside it.
115| \end{definition}
