150| \begin{proposition}[Baldwin's rules]\label{prop:b3:radicals-carbenes:baldwin}
151| For ring closures (established experimentally, with a stereoelectronic
152| rationale): at a tetrahedral carbon (tet), 3- to 7-exo are favoured, 5- and
153| 6-endo disfavoured; at a trigonal carbon (trig), 3- to 7-exo are favoured, 3- to 5-endo
154| disfavoured, 6- and 7-endo favoured; at a digonal carbon (dig), 3- and 4-exo are
155| disfavoured, 5- to 7-exo favoured, 3- to 7-endo favoured.
156| \end{proposition}
157| 
158| The rationale is the angle of attack each kind of bond needs: from the back of
159| the bond at a tet carbon, at about 107° to a trigonal $\pi$ system, at a narrower
160| angle to a triple bond; a short chain cannot reach those positions for the
161| disfavoured cases.
